# Applied migrations are checksummed BY BYTE, so their line endings are part of
# the contract.
#
# Prisma records a SHA-256 of each migration file when it applies it, and warns
# that the migration "was modified after it was applied" when the bytes on disk
# no longer hash to the recorded value. Its offer to resolve that is to reset
# the development database.
#
# Without this rule, a checkout on Windows rewrites every `.sql` to CRLF and
# every one of those checksums changes — so a developer who has migrated on one
# machine and cloned on another is told their history was tampered with, and
# invited to drop their database over a line ending. Pinning LF makes the file
# the same bytes everywhere.
*.sql text eol=lf
